My apologies for the confusion. To make the sublist of sales order search results selectable, you need to add a client script to the Sales Order page. Here is an example of how you can achieve this:
```javascript
/**
 * @NApiVersion 2.x
 * @NScriptType ClientScript
 * @NModuleScope SameAccount
 */

define(['N/currentRecord'], function(currentRecord) {
  function pageInit(context) {
    var currRec = currentRecord.get();

    if (currRec.type === 'salesorder' && currRec.mode === 'edit') {
      // Get the sublist object
      var sublist = currRec.getSublist({ sublistId: 'item' });

      // Add an event listener to the sublist
      sublist.on('click', function(event) {
        // Get the selected line number
        var line = event.line;

        // Set the line as selected
        sublist.selectLine({ line: line });
      });
    }
  }

  return {
    pageInit: pageInit
  };
});
```
In this example, the client script is added to the Sales Order page and it listens to the `pageInit` event. When the page is initialized, the script checks if the current record is a Sales Order in edit mode. If it is, the script gets the `item` sublist object and adds an event listener to it.

When a user clicks on a line in the sublist, the script gets the line number and sets it as selected using the `selectLine` method.

You can customize this script further to meet your specific requirements, such as updating the selected line when a user clicks on the line again or adding validation to prevent users from selecting certain lines.

