function pageInit() {
  var sublist = document.getElementById('custpage_sublist');
  sublist.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
    var recordId = e.target.dataset.recordId;
    if (recordId) {
      var url = nlapiResolveURL('RECORD', 'salesorder', recordId, 'VIEW');
      window.open(url);
    }
  });
}
```
This code adds a click event listener to the sublist table with an ID of "custpage\_sublist". When a row in the table is clicked, the record ID of the clicked row is retrieved from the "data-record-id" attribute of the clicked element. If the attribute is present, the script opens the record in a new window using the `nlapiResolveURL()` function.

Make sure to add the `pageInit()` function to your Suitelet script and also include a reference to your client script using the `nlapiLoadFile()` function. For example:
```javascript
function suitelet(request, response) {
  var form = nlapiCreateForm('Sales Order Search');

  // Add filters and sublist to the form

  // Load client script
  var clientScript = nlapiLoadFile('SuiteScripts/MyClientScript.js');
  form.setScript('customscript_mysuitelet', clientScript);

  // Display the form
  response.writePage(form);
}

